Return an error for a Content-Length that is not a number.

The parse was unwrapped, so one request with a header such as
`Content-Length: abc` panicked the server before any handler ran.
The body type is now resolved fallibly and the failure surfaces as
a headers error, which `Connection::new` returns to its caller.

